id: befriend
name: Befriend
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Persuasion
requiresSkill: persuasion
requiresRanks: 2
# "Session Limit: Infinite."
sessionLimit: infinite
timeCost: Instant
# "Target a Character you can see or speak to. Make a Clash (Persuasion vs Intuition/Persuasion)."
clashSkill: persuasion
clashDefenderSkills: intuition, persuasion
# "You cannot target the same Character twice with the Befriend Maneuver in an Adventuring Session (or
# while they are still influenced by its effects)."
oncePerTarget: true
# "If you win, increase your Affection Rating for that Character by 1 for 1 Day." Affection Ratings are
# not in this system: said on the card, {challenger} and {defender} named.
clashWinNote: {challenger}'s Affection Rating for {defender} is 1 higher for 1 Day
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Persuasion Clash against someone's Intuition or Persuasion: win, and your Affection Rating for them
  is 1 higher for a day. Once for each Character in an Adventuring Session.
text: >
  Befriend: You convince someone that you are on the same side as them.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Persuasion
  –Session Limit: Infinite
  –Time Cost: Instant
  –Effect: Target a Character you can see or speak to. Make a Clash (Persuasion vs
  Intuition/Persuasion) against them. If you win, increase your Affection Rating for that Character by 1
  for 1 Day. You cannot target the same Character twice with the Befriend Maneuver in an Adventuring
  Session (or while they are still influenced by its effects).

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Persuasion, with no Session Limit. Used at the
# one token targeted - refused if they were already Befriended this Adventuring Session - and the Clash
# card opens at once. Won, the card says the Affection Rating: those are not built, so keeping it, the
# day it lasts, and a Character still influenced into the next Session are the table's.
